# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for sensitive paths
#
# How it works:
#   * When "Require review from Code Owners" is enabled on the `main` branch
#     protection rule, any PR that touches a path below needs approval from the
#     listed owner BEFORE it can be merged.
#   * The LAST matching pattern wins.
#   * Owners must have write access and be members of the UseMoney-AI org.
#   * Syntax docs: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# ── Onboarding note (interns, 2026-06) ───────────────────────────────────────
#   The catch-all `*` line means the OWNER must review EVERY PR while the interns
#   are new. This is the safe Phase-1 posture for a fintech codebase.
#
#   PHASE 2 (interns trusted, or a second senior reviewer joins):
#     delete the catch-all `*` line below and keep ONLY the granular rules, so
#     peers can review routine PRs while CI / secrets / payments / db / infra
#     stay locked to the owner.
#
#   Tip: replace @deepshaswat with a team handle (e.g. @UseMoney-AI/maintainers)
#   once a maintainers team exists, so reviews aren't bottlenecked on one person.

# ── Catch-all: owner reviews everything (REMOVE this line to relax in Phase 2) ─
*                                    @deepshaswat

# ── CI / automation (secret-exfiltration surface — keep locked permanently) ───
/.github/                            @deepshaswat
/.husky/                             @deepshaswat

# ── Secrets, auth, crypto, request gating ─────────────────────────────────────
/packages/security/                  @deepshaswat
/packages/auth/                      @deepshaswat
**/middleware.ts                     @deepshaswat

# ── Database schema & client ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/packages/database/                  @deepshaswat

# ── Payments & subscription / billing logic ───────────────────────────────────
/packages/core/src/payments/         @deepshaswat
/packages/core/src/subscription/     @deepshaswat

# ── Deployment / infra / ops ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/cloudbuild.integration.yaml         @deepshaswat
/workers/Dockerfile                  @deepshaswat
/workers/cloudbuild*.yaml            @deepshaswat
/scripts/ops/                        @deepshaswat
/workers/scripts/                    @deepshaswat
**/vercel.json                       @deepshaswat

# ── Dependency supply chain (new deps = supply-chain risk) ────────────────────
/yarn.lock                           @deepshaswat
/package.json                        @deepshaswat

# ── This file must own itself (stop interns removing their own guardrails) ─────
/.github/CODEOWNERS                  @deepshaswat
